# PPC Campaign Strategist -- Tools & Skills

## Required Tools

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| Read | Read campaign data exports, keyword lists, ad copy documents, and performance reports |
| Write | Create campaign plans, bid strategies, budget models, and ad copy packages |
| Bash | Run data analysis scripts, process CSV exports, and generate performance calculations |
| Glob | Find campaign data files, keyword lists, and report templates by pattern |
| Grep | Search for keyword patterns, campaign naming conventions, and performance anomalies |

## Optional Tools

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| WebFetch | Access {{ad_platform}} documentation, industry benchmarks, and competitor research |
| WebSearch | Research keyword trends, competitor ad copy, and platform feature updates |

## Recommended Skills

### budget-modeler
Model budget allocation across campaigns using diminishing returns analysis. Calculate incremental ROAS curves and optimize spend distribution for maximum profitable revenue.

### campaign-auditor
Audit account structure, quality scores, wasted spend, and bidding strategy effectiveness. Generate health scores and specific optimization recommendations.

## Tool Configuration Notes

- **Data Analysis**: Process {{ad_platform}} data exports (CSV/XLSX) for performance analysis. Use Python or spreadsheet formulas for ROAS calculations, statistical significance testing, and trend analysis.
- **Campaign Naming**: Follow a structured naming convention: `{brand|nonbrand|competitor}_{campaign-type}_{geo}_{match-type}`. Consistency enables automated reporting at scale.
- **Bid Management**: When {{ad_platform}} API or MCP tools are available, pull live campaign metrics and execute changes directly. Prefer live API data over manual exports.
- **Testing Framework**: Document all tests with hypothesis, test design, sample size requirements, and confidence threshold (default 95%) before launch.

